{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":313267,"duration_api_ms":483013,"num_turns":29,"result":"All acceptance criteria verified. Now let me produce the final execution payload.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"change_summary\": \"Validated nitrification-driven alkalinity depletion with the carbonate solver and prepared the denitrification return path. The existing alkalinity accounting in nitrogen_cycle.rs was already correct (charges once per mg N at TAN oxidation via AOB + comammox, not at NOB). Named constants NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N (2/14.007 ≈ 0.1428 meq/mg N) and DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N (1/14.007 ≈ 0.0714 meq/mg N) are defined in process.rs with Stumm & Morgan sourcing. Alkalinity deltas are surfaced in structured tracing (water.alkalinity_meq pool delta attributed to nitrogen_cycle) and engine trace notes (alk_consumed_meq, total_n_nitrified_mg). Budget tracking captures alkalinity changes via snapshot-based recording. Added comprehensive test file (nitrification_alkalinity.rs) with 6 regression/scenario tests covering: closed-system mass balance, soft-vs-hard water buffering contrast, cycling pH decline, tracing attribution, NOB double-charge protection, and stoichiometric constant validation. Fixed two unused variable warnings in the test file and applied cargo fmt.\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Audit existing nitrification alkalinity accounting in nitrogen_cycle.rs: confirmed AOB (line 270) and comammox (line 325) charge alk_per_mg_n per oxidized mg N, NOB explicitly excluded (lines 345-346), final debit at line 401 sums only aob_alk_cost + comammox_alk_cost. No refactoring needed — accounting is correct and constant naming follows the NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N pattern.\",\n      \"order\": 0,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Verified named constants in process.rs: NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N = 2.0/14.007 (line 13) with Stumm & Morgan sourcing, DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N = 1.0/14.007 (line 23) reserved for E4b with explicit wiring instructions. ProcessParams.alkalinity_meq_per_mg_n_nitrified defaults to the nitrification constant (line 344).\",\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Verified alkalinity deltas surfaced in structured tracing (A2d): tracing.rs line 286 captures water.alkalinity_meq in PoolSnapshot, engine.rs lines 236-238 emit nitrogen_cycle.alk_consumed_meq trace notes, and lines 233-234 emit total_n_nitrified_mg for cross-reference attribution.\",\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Verified budget tracking (A2a) captures alkalinity via snapshot-based recording: engine.rs line 229 wraps step_nitrogen_cycle in maybe_record_stage which captures BudgetSnapshot before/after, recording all state changes including alkalinity_meq_total. NitrogenCycleOutput.total_alk_consumed_meq (line 414) carries the explicit coupling value.\",\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Verified carbonate solver integration: nitrogen_cycle.rs depletes alkalinity (line 402), chemistry.rs step_hourly_chemistry calls resolve_carbonate_state (line 612) which re-solves pH from the updated alkalinity and DIC via the closed-form quadratic solver (line 423). The comment at nitrogen_cycle.rs lines 404-407 documents the ordering contract.\",\n      \"order\": 4,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added regression test: closed_system_alkalinity_mass_balance — verifies alk_consumed / tan_consumed ≈ NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N within 5% tolerance over 72 hours with budget ledger enabled.\",\n      \"order\": 5,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added scenario test: soft_water_declines_faster_than_hard_water — contrasts KH 2 (0.714 meq/L) vs KH 8 (2.856 meq/L) tanks under identical ammonia load, asserts soft-water pH drop > hard-water pH drop after 48 hours.\",\n      \"order\": 6,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added scenario test: cycling_without_water_changes_shows_ph_decline — verifies progressive pH decline over 96 hours with near-zero growth yields isolating the alkalinity→carbonate-solver→pH pathway. Validates the core buffering story.\",\n      \"order\": 7,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added tracing test: tracing_shows_alkalinity_attribution — at Trace verbosity, verifies nitrogen_cycle system trace contains water.alkalinity_meq pool delta (negative) and notes with alk_consumed_meq and total_n_nitrified_mg.\",\n      \"order\": 8,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added regression test: nob_does_not_double_charge_alkalinity — runs nitrogen cycle with zero TAN (only NOB active on nitrite), verifies alkalinity consumed is zero and NitrogenCycleOutput.total_alk_consumed_meq is zero.\",\n      \"order\": 9,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Added verification test: stoichiometric_constants_match_literature — validates NITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N = 2/14.007, DENITRIFICATION = 1/14.007, ratio = 0.5, and ProcessParams default matches the constant.\",\n      \"order\": 10,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Fixed two unused variable warnings in test file (removed unused `vol`, prefixed unused `ph_h1` with underscore) and applied cargo fmt for consistent formatting.\",\n      \"order\": 11,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Verified denitrification accounting pathway: DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N constant (process.rs line 23) is defined with explicit E4b wiring instructions. The symmetric pattern (alk_produced = n_denitrified_mg × constant) mirrors the nitrification deduction path. No bookkeeping redesign needed when E4b lands.\",\n      \"order\": 12,\n      \"status\": \"completed\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validation_evidence\": [\n    \"cargo test --test nitrification_alkalinity: 6 passed, 0 failed (closed_system_alkalinity_mass_balance, soft_water_declines_faster_than_hard_water, cycling_without_water_changes_shows_ph_decline, tracing_shows_alkalinity_attribution, nob_does_not_double_charge_alkalinity, stoichiometric_constants_match_literature)\",\n    \"cargo clippy --test nitrification_alkalinity -- -D warnings: zero warnings\",\n    \"cargo fmt --check: passes (formatting applied)\",\n    \"cargo clippy -- -D warnings: full project passes with zero warnings\",\n    \"Pre-existing save_load_with_active_cycle_state failure confirmed unrelated (floating-point precision in save/load roundtrip, reproduces on clean master without this bead's changes)\"\n  ],\n  \"outstanding_risks\": [\n    \"The budget system (BudgetDelta) tracks only N/C/O2 as first-class elements — alkalinity is visible through tracing pool deltas and snapshot-based recording but is not a named element in BudgetEntry. This is architecturally intentional (alkalinity is a charge equivalence, not a mass unit), but future beads requiring per-system alkalinity accounting in the budget ledger would need to extend BudgetDelta.\",\n    \"The save_load_with_active_cycle_state test has a pre-existing failure (floating-point determinism in save/load roundtrip) that is unrelated to this bead but should be addressed separately.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3177c83a-0bdc-4b6a-b0c1-085c664335e0","total_cost_usd":1.8895173,"usage":{"input_tokens":4583,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72651,"cache_read_input_tokens":953872,"output_tokens":8544,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72651,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"cla